+    summary: Engine model inventory and lifecycle
+    text: '## Engine model inventory and lifecycle
+
+
+      Use the `Readio` gateway for normalized engine-model records and explicit lifecycle
+      actions. Its public methods are `Readio.list_models()`, `Readio.model_status()`,
+      `Readio.install_model()`, `Readio.update_model()`, `Readio.verify_model()`, and
+      `Readio.remove_model()`. The inventory is read-only: it does not install, download,
+      load, verify, or inspect engine caches.
+
+
+      ```python
+
+      from readio.api import Readio
+
+
+      service = Readio()
+
+      models = service.list_models("kitten", language="en-US", offline=True)
+
+      status = service.model_status("kitten", "kitten-v1", quality="high")
+
+      ```
+
+
+      `EngineModelInfo` is a Readio-owned DTO with `ModelState` and `ModelUpdateState`
+      fields. `state` is mapped only from recognized, consistent VoiceRender status
+      values; unknown or inconsistent status remains `unknown`. `update_state` is `unknown`
+      when no authoritative comparison was reported. Version strings are provider-defined,
+      and byte counts or storage identity remain `None` when the provider does not report
+      them. False availability/action flags mean VoiceRender did not assert that capability,
+      not that Readio independently checked it.
+
+
+      `install_model()`, `verify_model()`, and `remove_model()` are explicit operations
+      delegated to VoiceRender. They return normalized status, re-querying when an operation
+      result has no usable model descriptor. The current VoiceRender public API has
+      no authoritative update operation, so `update_model()` raises `ModelOperationError`;
+      it never aliases to force-install. Existing module-level `list_engine_models()`,
+      `inspect_engine_model()`, and operation delegates remain specialist-result compatibility
+      APIs.
+
+
+
+      `engine_models_to_dict()` and `serialize_public()` use the versioned `readio.engine-models.v1`
+      envelope, containing only normalized Readio fields.'
