+    summary: Engine model inventory and lifecycle
+    text: "## Engine model inventory and lifecycle
+
+
+      VoiceRender owns synthesis engine packages, model registries, model storage, revision
+      semantics, downloads, verification, and removal. Readio normalizes public VoiceRender
+      model records and delegates explicit model actions. Readio does not mutate Python
+      package environments, inspect specialist-private caches, guess storage paths,
+      or delete model directories.
+
+
+      The stable application contract is `readio.api.EngineModelInfo` with `Readio.list_models()`,
+      `Readio.model_status()`, `Readio.install_model()`, `Readio.verify_model()`, and
+      `Readio.remove_model()`. VoiceRender 0.2.12 does not publish byte counts, stable
+      storage identity, per-model action capabilities, or authoritative update semantics;
+      Readio leaves those values unknown or unasserted. `Readio.update_model()` reports
+      unsupported operation rather than treating force-install as update. Existing module-level
+      delegates preserve their VoiceRender-native results for compatibility."
