+    summary: Engine model inventory and lifecycle
+    text: "### Engine model inventory and lifecycle
+
+
+      Model commands use normalized Readio output for human-readable results:
+
+
+      ```bash
+
+      readio models list --engine kitten --lang en-US
+
+      readio models show kitten-v1 --engine kitten --quality high
+
+      readio models install kitten-v1 --engine kitten
+
+      readio models verify kitten-v1 --engine kitten
+
+      readio models remove kitten-v1 --engine kitten --yes
+
+      ```
+
+
+      The human inventory columns are `ENGINE`, `TARGET`, `QUALITY`, `STATE`, `LOCAL
+      VERSION`, `AVAILABLE VERSION`, `SIZE`, and `UPDATE`. Missing provider metadata
+      appears as `-` or `unknown`. VoiceRender owns model storage and revision semantics;
+      Readio does not inspect engine caches or install Python distributions.
+
+
+      For compatibility, `--json` without `--normalized-json` retains the existing VoiceRender-native
+      JSON result. Use `--normalized-json` on any model command to request the normalized
+      `readio.engine-models.v1` envelope; the flag implies JSON output. VoiceRender
+      0.2.12 does not provide authoritative update semantics, so there is no `models
+      update` command and the API reports update as unsupported rather than force-installing."
